Title:
VulnFanatic-NG — LLM-assisted vulnerability research for Binary Ninja

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4–8 sentences max):
VulnFanatic-NG is a Binary Ninja plugin that scans decompiled binaries and uses an LLM (local OpenAI-compatible by default, or Claude/Gemini/Azure) to decide whether suspicious patterns are real vulnerabilities. It focuses on HLIL decompiler output, builds large interprocedural context (types, value ranges, stack layout, call paths, def-use chains, path constraints), and asks the model for a structured JSON verdict, reporting only confirmed issues with clickable navigation back to code. Phase 1 targets dangerous API call sites (overflows, format strings, command execution, weak RNG, SQLi, TLS verify disabled, UAF/double-free, privilege misuse, etc.), Phase 2 audits security-sensitive code when symbols/strings indicate auth/crypto/session/validation logic, and Phase 3 (opt-in, online-only) checks firmware hardening controls against fault-injection/side-channel classes. It includes an offline (no-LLM) heuristic mode for fast triage and a two-pass “validation” mode using a second model to reduce false positives. Findings can be triaged in the UI and exported as OpenAI chat JSONL for iterative fine-tuning (includes an MLX LoRA fine-tune script for Apple Silicon). Useful for reverse engineers, vuln researchers, and red teams doing binary auditing at scale, with explicit attention to context quality and auditability (scratchpad + confidence).

Technical Focus:
- Binary Ninja HLIL/MLIL-based static analysis and call-site discovery (incl. PLT/thunks and indirect calls)
- Interprocedural context construction (call paths, def-use tracing, type/struct sizing, stack layout, value-set analysis)
- Rule-driven detection of dangerous APIs and security-sensitive functionality (JSON rule packs)
- LLM structured-output verdicting, confidence scoring, and optional second-pass validation
- Offline heuristic scanning and safe-elimination logic (constant args, bounded ranges, guard detection)
- Triage workflow + export for model fine-tuning (OpenAI JSONL, MLX LoRA)

Use Cases:
- Rapid triage of large binaries for likely memory corruption and injection primitives
- Auditing call sites of risky libc/Win32 APIs with decompiler-aware context (buffer sizes, argument provenance)
- Reviewing authentication/crypto/session/token code paths when symbols or string evidence exist
- Firmware/security-module hardening reviews for glitching/side-channel mitigation gaps (Phase 3)
- Building organization-specific vulnerability-review datasets and fine-tuning a local code model

Keywords:
Binary Ninja, HLIL, MLIL, decompiler, static analysis, interprocedural analysis, def-use, value-set analysis, stack layout, PLT thunks, indirect calls, function pointers, vtable, LLM, OpenAI-compatible API, Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, Azure OpenAI, structured JSON output, buffer overflow, format string, command injection, SQL injection, use-after-free, double free, TLS certificate verification, firmware hardening, fault injection, side-channel, LoRA, MLX, fine-tuning JSONL